# CloudBSD Application Guidelines

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root. It is the authoritative, tool-neutral
statement of CloudBSD law, and it links to every guideline document you must
read before generating code, configuration, or documentation.

Then read `Agent-Behavior/AGENT_BEHAVIOR.md` for how to work: think before
coding, keep it simple, keep changes surgical, define verifiable success
criteria.

For a task-specific skill, scan `SKILLS/TOC.md` and load the single `SKILL.md`
that matches. Do not load the whole tree.

This file carries no rules of its own. If a rule needs to change, change
`AGENTS.md`.
